{"labs": [{"stimuli": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "_data": []}, {"id": 1, "template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "enpe7n6le02ob09re2aud01", "coverimg": "enpe7n6le02ob09re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"id": 0, "image": "enpe7n6le02ob09re2img01.jpg", "text": "<b>Karen</b>: I haven't studied for the next programming exam, what about you? <br>\n<b>Brian</b>: Neither have I.  Is it about constants? <br>\n<b>Karen</b>: No, it's about Operators, but I didn't understand the teacher's explanation. <br>\n<b>Brian</b>: Neither did I. This teacher doesn't explain as well as Mrs. Patterson. However, if you want, we can study together. I have some information that can help us. <br>\n<b>Karen</b>: Sure, so let's start! <br>\n<b>Brian</b>: So, what do you think PHP operators mean? <br>\n<b>Karen</b>: What I understood is that these are conventions to express mathematical operations.  <br>\n<b>Brian</b>: Yes! In PHP, these are conventions or symbols that permit us to perform specific functions on variables and values such as addition, multiplication, subtraction, concatenation, among others.", "time": "0"}, {"id": 1, "image": "enpe7n6le02ob09re2img02.jpg", "text": "<b>Karen</b>: That's not as tough as I thought. <br>\n<b>Brian</b>: Indeed, it is easy. <br>\n<b>Karen</b>: Is that all, right? <br>\n<b>Brian</b>:  No, we still have the types of PHP Operators. <br>\n<b>Karen</b>: Well, I learned about the Arithmetic Operators. You can use them with numeric values to carry out arithmetical operations such as addition, division, exponentiation, among others.  I guess there are two or three more types of PHP operators. <br>\n<b>Brian</b>: No, including Arithmetical operators, there are seven types: Assignment, Comparison, Increment/Decrement, Logical, String, and Array operators.", "time": "58000"}, {"id": 2, "image": "enpe7n6le02ob09re2img03.jpg", "text": "<b>Karen</b>: Well, I know that the Assignment operation is in charge of using numeric values and converts them into written values. Then, the Comparison operator is used to contrast two values. Do we need to learn the function of each operator? <br>\n<b>Brian</b>: No, it's not necessary. We didn't study that in class, so it won't be included.<br>\n<b>Karen</b>: Let's hope so because learning the function of each operator is not as effortless as their general characteristics. <br>\n<b>Brian</b>: You're right. I won't study that. <br>\n<b>Karen</b>: So, neither will I.", "time": "105000"}]}}], "_data": []}, {"id": 2, "template_override": 1, "type": "static", "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "img", "value": "01.jpg"}, {"type": "img", "value": "02.jpg"}, {"type": "img", "value": "03.jpg"}, {"type": "img", "value": "04.jpg"}, {"type": "img", "value": "05.jpg"}, {"type": "img", "value": "06.jpg"}, {"type": "img", "value": "07.jpg"}], "_data": []}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "img_path": "", "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "I can list the operators used in PHP.   ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can explain what PHP operators mean.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Do you know how to compare two values? Explain. ", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "Have you ever used numeric values to perform arithmetical operations? Explain. ", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct"}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content":