 [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "What Does PHP Operators mean?", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 9, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "You can use these words to talk about PHP Operators. ", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Understand information about web applications, their principles and basic concepts in a range of work contexts.   Describe applications for an operating system for personal computers in a range of work contexts. ", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.\t Exchanges simple information on web applications, and applications for operating systems for personal computers.", "type": "secondary_1"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le02ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Comparisons with as - As", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "We use <strong>as \u2013 as</strong> when we make a statement in which two things or people share a quality.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<strong>As \u2013 as</strong> is a form to make comparisons. The rule is that between <strong>as \u2013 as</strong> we must write an adjective or adverb. </br></br> Examples:<span class=\"italic\"></br> PHP Operators are not <b>as complicated as </b>Constants.</br> The Comparison operator doesn't have <b>as many operations as </b> the Arithmetical operator.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "That's not as tough as I believed. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Let's hope so because learning the function of each operator is not as effortless as their general characteristics. ", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Responses with Neither", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When we want to agree to a person's negative statement, saying that we don't do or we don't like the same thing, we use<strong> neither.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The rule is to make this answer in the same time tense. </br></br> Examples: </br><br> Present  <span class=\"italic\">    </br> A: I <b>don't work </b>with PHP operators. </br> B: <b>Neither do I.</b></br></br></span>  Past</br><span class=\"italic\">     A: I <b>didn't know </b>how to use the Logical operators. </br> B: <b>Neither did I.</b></br></br>   </span>  Future</br><span class=\"italic\">     A: I <b>won't study </b>for tomorrow's test</br> B: Really? <b>Neither will I.</b></br>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<b>Karen</b>: I haven't studied for the next programming exam, what about you? <br> <b>Brian</b>: Neither have I.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<b>Brian</b>: You're right. I won't study that. <br> <b>Karen</b>: So, neither will I.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "concatenation", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an operation of linking character strings", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: These are conventions or symbols that permit us to perform specific functions on variables and values such as addition, multiplication, subtraction, concatenation, among others.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le02ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "tough", "type": "name"}, {"content": "related to difficult ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: That's not as tough as I believed.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le02ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "carry out ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to perform .", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(phrasal verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You can use them with numeric values to carry out arithmetical operations. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le02ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "exponentiation ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "algorithm used to raise an specific quantity to the power of another one", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You can use them with numeric values to carry out arithmetical operations such as addition, division, among others. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le02ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "effortless", "type": "name"}, {"content": "easy to do ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Learning the function of each operator is not as effortless as their general characteristics.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le02ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Investigate about conditional statements in PHP", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down your findings with the vocabulary of PHP conditional statements ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a presentation for your classmates and teacher", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I can investigate about more PHP operators ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I can write about more PHP operators ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I can talk about PHP operators", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}]}